# A permutation model of the Suzuki sporadic group `Suz`

This file defines a permutation model `TauCeti.Sporadic.Suz` of the Suzuki sporadic group `Suz`:
the subgroup of `Equiv.Perm (Fin 1782)` generated by six explicit permutations `Suz.a`, …,
`Suz.f`, five of order `3` and one, `Suz.d`, of order `10`. The Suzuki group has a maximal
subgroup `G₂(4)` of index `1782`, the least degree in which it acts faithfully, and on its cosets
it acts as a group of rank `3` with suborbits of lengths `1`, `416` and `1365`; the model is meant
as that action.

The six permutations are given by their tables of images, and the point `i` of `Fin 1782` is the
point `i` of the source of the tables (see *Provenance*). Products follow Mathlib's convention
`(σ * τ) x = σ (τ x)`.

Neither the order of the model nor its transitivity or simplicity is asserted here. The module
`TauCeti.GroupTheory.SpecificGroups.Sporadic.Suzuki.Presentation` gives seven involutions that
generate the model and satisfy the relators of the presentation selected for `Suz`, and so maps
the presented group onto the model.

## Main declarations

* `TauCeti.Sporadic.Suz`: the permutation model of the Suzuki sporadic group on `1782` points.
* `TauCeti.Sporadic.Suz.orderOf_a`, …, `TauCeti.Sporadic.Suz.orderOf_f`: the orders of the six
  generators, which are `3`, `3`, `3`, `10`, `3` and `3`.

## Provenance

The tables of `Suz.a`, …, `Suz.f` are those of the permutations `SuzPerm.suza`, …,
`SuzPerm.suzf` of the `FiniteSimpleGroups` project (Apache-2.0), files
`FiniteSimpleGroups/Sporadic/Suz/PermSuza.lean`, …, `PermSuzf.lean` at commit
`7f09e33a9ceef6b59ce03e34cd4f0558c763e325`, and the model is the subgroup `SuzGroup.SuzSubgroup`
of `FiniteSimpleGroups/Sporadic/Suz/SuzGroup.lean` that they generate there. The source stores the
images of the points `0`, …, `1781` under `suza` as the concatenation of the lists
`suzaFwdChunk0`, …, `suzaFwdChunk13`, and likewise for the other five generators and for the
preimages (`suzaInvChunk0`, …); entry `i` of a table below is entry `i` of that concatenation, so
the numbering of the points is unchanged. Only the table of preimages of `suzd` is reproduced:
the other five generators have order `3`, and their inverses are their squares. The source
describes the points as the vertices of a graph on `1782` points which the six permutations
preserve: one distinguished point, the `416` points of an orbit of `G₂(4)`, and a family of `1365`
further points. The definitions of the six permutations are taken from the source; its proofs of
the order and the simplicity of the generated group are not reproduced here.

## References

* KitaKen1 (Kenta), *FiniteSimpleGroups*, `Suz` construction at commit
  `7f09e33a9ceef6b59ce03e34cd4f0558c763e325`,
  <https://github.com/KitaKen1/finite-simple-groups-lean>.
* R. A. Wilson, R. A. Parker, J. N. Bray et al., *ATLAS of Finite Group Representations*,
  version 3, the page of `Suz`, for the maximal subgroup `G₂(4)` of index `1782`,
  <https://brauer.maths.qmul.ac.uk/Atlas/v3/spor/Suz/>.
