/- Each generator is given by the table of its images. A table has 60 rows, each a hexadecimal
numeral holding 30 entries of three digits (the last row holds the remaining 12): the entry of
the point `30 * r + j` is the group of three digits of row `r` in position `j` counted from the
right, starting at zero. The table is the natural number having the rows as its digits in base
`2 ^ 360`, so that the entry of the point `i` is field `i` of width `12` of that number. The
kernel reads such a field by binary arithmetic in one step, whereas a lookup in a list or an
array costs one reduction for every position passed.

The bodies are exposed so that importing modules can compute with the six permutations. -/

